        "original_id": "7a17970e-c8fd-5cbf-a0da-3feb26c88f60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Kouf, Ed O'Neill, Fred Gwynne, Lou Diamond Phillips, Rubén Blades, William Russ, Corbin Bernsen, Daniel Roebuck, Hoyt Axton\n- Films: Disorganized Crime\n- Companies: Touchstone Pictures, Fox Network, ABC\n- TV Shows: Married... with Children, Modern Family\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Primetime Emmy Awards, Screen Actors Guild Awards\n\nFacts:\n- Ed O'Neill was born on April 12, 1946, and he is an American actor and comedian.\n- Disorganized Crime is a 1989 American heist comedy film written and directed by Jim Kouf and released through Touchstone Pictures.\n- The ensemble cast of Disorganized Crime includes Fred Gwynne, Lou Diamond Phillips, Rubén Blades, William Russ, Corbin Bernsen, Ed O'Neill, Daniel Roebuck, and Hoyt Axton.\n- Ed O'Neill is best known for playing Al Bundy on the Fox Network sitcom Married... with Children, a role that earned him two Golden Globe nominations.\n- Ed O'Neill also played Jay Pritchett on the ABC sitcom Modern Family, a role that brought him three Primetime Emmy Award nominations and four Screen Actors Guild Awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
